.TH DSHUF 1 dshuf\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dshuf \- suckless multi-key low-discrepancy shuffler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dshuf
.RB [ \-Shvz ]
.RB [ \-k
.IR field[:weight] ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR delim ]
.RB [ \-j
.IR jitter ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR window ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR seed ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR count ]
.RI [ file\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dshuf
shuffles lines from standard input or files using low-discrepancy spacing with controllable jitter.
It solves the clustering and starvation problems of standard random shuffling by separating items
that share attribute keys (such as artist, album, or genre) while preserving pseudo-randomness.
.P
If no
.I file
operands are specified, or if a file operand is
.BR \- ,
.B dshuf
reads from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-k " field[:weight]"
Specify a 1-based column index to cluster on, and an optional floating-point repulsion weight (default 1.0 for primary, decaying for subsequent keys).
This option may be given multiple times to configure multi-key hierarchical clustering.
.TP
.BI \-d " delim"
Set the field delimiter character (default is tab \fB\\t\fR).
.TP
.BI \-j " jitter"
Tune the randomness factor between 0.0 (strictly optimal spacing) and 1.0 (pure random shuffle). Default is 0.20.
.TP
.BI \-w " window"
Set the sliding window buffer size for distance tracking and streaming mode. Default is 256.
.TP
.B \-S
Force streaming mode. Emits lines through the sliding window as they arrive from input without loading the entire stream into memory.
.TP
.BI \-s " seed"
Set an explicit 64-bit seed for deterministic, reproducible shuffles. If omitted, entropy is read from /dev/urandom or system timers.
.TP
.BI \-n " count"
Output at most
.I count
lines.
.TP
.B \-z
Treat input and output lines as terminated by a NUL byte rather than a newline.
.TP
.B \-v
Print version information to standard error and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage summary to standard error and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Shuffle a tab-separated music collection by artist (column 1):
.IP
.B dshuf -k 1 playlist.tsv
.PP
Multi-key shuffle by artist (col 1) and album (col 2) with custom weights:
.IP
.B dshuf -k 1:1.0 -k 2:0.5 playlist.tsv
.PP
Stream an endless pipe with bounded memory:
.IP
.B cat stream.tsv | dshuf -k 1 -S -w 128
.PP
Reproducible shuffle using an explicit seed:
.IP
.B dshuf -k 1 -s 1337 playlist.tsv
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shuf (1),
.BR sort (1),
.BR cut (1)
